<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Colón, Panama</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aspinwall</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Colón is a port city at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> entrance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal">Panama Canal</a> and Panama's second city. Founded in 1850 as the Atlantic terminus of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-railroad">Panama Railroad</a> and first called Aspinwall by the Americans, it grew with the railway and canal and was rebuilt after a great fire in 1885. It is home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colon-free-zone">Colón Free Zone</a>, created in 1948, one of the largest free-trade zones in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/colon-panama.jpg" alt="Colón, Panama" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Balou46 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CO-colon-2000-02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
